# surfcontext.org

The official documentation site for **SurfContext** — the open standard for agent-ready
project documentation (ARDS v5.2).

The specification itself lives in `SPEC.surf` at the repository root. The `/spec` page is
a rendered view of that file, so the site can never drift from the ratified text.

## Development

```bash
cargo run
```

Open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000). Set `PORT` to listen elsewhere.

## Build and test

```bash
cargo build --locked
cargo test --locked
bash tools/ards-tests.sh
python3 tools/ards-lint.py
```

## Stack

- Rust (edition 2024) with Axum 0.8 and Tokio
- `surf-parse` for SurfDoc rendering
- Fly.io for deployment

## Repository layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `SPEC.surf` | The ARDS specification — canonical text |
| `CONTEXT.surf` | Root context for agents and contributors |
| `src/` | Axum server, routes, page shell |
| `content/` | Page source (`.surf`) |
| `tools/` | Linter, sync, hooks, tools battery |
| `templates/`, `playbooks/` | Starter templates and executable playbooks |

